Triplet Sum in Array:
Given an array arr[] and an integer target, determine if there exists a triplet in the array whose sum equals the given target.
Return true if such a triplet exists, otherwise, return false.

Explanation:
take a number - put it in a hahsmap inside the for loop 
calculate the needed2 ( which is basically the sum of other 2 nums)
again runa  for loop and check by needed = needed2- arr[i] (the last exisitng single number)
if it exisits in hashmap well and good
other wise it is false
just add the arr[j] to the hashmap

Code:
class Solution {
    public boolean hasTripletSum(int arr[], int target) {
        // code Here
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            int num = arr[i];
            HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
            int needed2 = target - num;
            
            for(int j=i+1;j<arr.length;j++){
                int needed3 = needed2 - arr[j];
                if(map.containsKey(needed3)){
                    return true;
                }
                map.put(arr[j],1);
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}
